## Microsoft.Pex.Framework 

The framework provides the execution framework to run Pex tests. It includes a set of PInvoke calls for interacting with the runtime of the managed test and providing the necessary services that Pex requires.

It’s typically used as part of the test target.

## Microsoft.Pex.Common

The common library includes common features and interfaces required by Pex to run tests. It includes classes for exception, PInvoke call, and CLR metadata information.

It’s typically used as part of the test target, analysis tool, or verification tool.

## Microsoft.Pex.Interpreter

The interpreter library analyzes the specified source code files and generates execution plans for testing those files.

It’s typically used as part of the test target or analysis tool.

## Microsoft.Pex.Search

The search library includes classes that form the core of Pex’s search algorithm.

It’s typically used as part of the test target or analysis tool.

## Microsoft.Pex.Targets

The MSBuild targets are assembly dependencies required by Pex to enable integration with MSBuild during testing. 

It’s typically used as part of the build process.


## Microsoft.Pex.Triage

The triage library provides the framework to manage and prioritize the Pex search work items. 

It’s typically used as part of the analysis tool.


## Microsoft.Pex.Visualization

The visualization library provides tools for displaying the results to users in a simple, easy-to-understand way. 

It’s typically used as part of the test target or analysis tool.



